3. Designer Notes

SGPE speed is not capped by reaction mass or exhaust velocity.

Maximum speed is limited only by:

anchor coherence

gradient stability

entropy saturation thresholds

structural tolerance of the craft

SGPE can exceed conventional propulsion limits because it does not push mass — it falls into stability.

4. White Sheet Summary

The Stability‑Gradient Propulsion Engine achieves motion by generating and amplifying stability gradients. Its speed is determined by gradient magnitude and entropy reinforcement. SGPE can operate from low‑drift maneuvering speeds to relativistic drift depending on configuration.

